  "question": {
    "text": "If the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> form an obtuse angle triangle (obtuse angled at angle <math><mi>A</mi></math>), then sum of all the possible integral values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is",
