  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, the point&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lie inside the circle whose end-points of the diameter are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, but does not lie on this diameter<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lie inside the circle <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />But,&nbsp;<math><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> because at <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, points <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are collinear<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Hence, the sum of all possible integral values of <math><mi>&#8216;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>&#8217;</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
